[h1]Phobos Shipbreaker[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.45.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Make the wreck pay for the next repair. Rivetline machinery brings wall processing, scrap recovery, metal casting and process water aboard, so a salvage run leaves you with stock, not just a hold full of panels.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]G4 Exterior Grabber, H4 Sealed Hull Chute and D4 Dismantling Fixture:[/b] break detached walls of any make, floor grates, DuraWal, Whipple and aero panels and windows into native scrap and parts. The products add up to the part's own mass.
[*][b]R4 Scrap Reclaimer:[/b] recovers steel and aluminium from identified panel residue. Rejects stay aboard and never yield more.
[*][b]F6 Electric Furnace:[/b] casts aluminium housings, aluminium ingots or steel ingots with electricity and one cooling assembly: direct cooling, or F6-C pipes to an exterior radiator. Hot metal stays sealed until safe release. Repeat batches can draw charges from a paired R4.
[*][b]C2 Residue Collector[/b] and storage unloading move residue and products over structural floor. A full store leaves cargo in the tray.
[*][b]S3, S4 and S5 Process Water Silos[/b] (1,000, 1,960 and 3,330 kg) and [b]T2 Ice Thaw Unit[/b]: thaw water ice into the silo, fill it at a station, or draw from Valtora's Ship's Water above a crew reserve. The game's ice asteroids now appear in new games, and methane ice yields water plus methane for a Manufacturing store.
[*][b]Y2, Y3 and Y4 Material Bins[/b] (INSTALL > FURN): sealed stores for ore, regolith, gangue, ice and mined chunks that crew orders fetch from and fill.
[*][b]G4 reclamation:[/b] with Auto Nav, capture an owned, empty, depressurized target and cut its ordinary walls. Recover valuables and crew first.
[*][b]Phobos' Asterel C1 Industrial Control Console[/b] runs equipment on your own ship from one seat. Crew orders can keep the D4, R4 and F6 loaded from anywhere aboard.
[/list]
Full names begin Phobos' Rivetline, for example Phobos' Rivetline F6 Electric Furnace.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Buy machinery at the K-Leg and VORB scrap suppliers (broken), the K-Leg fixer (used) or San Diego's Halvorson (new). Build smaller equipment and D4, R4 and F6 sections at an installed Bar or Dining Table, then assemble the machine on site through INSTALL > APPS. The silos, bins and T2 are purchase-only.
[*]Arrange grabber, chute and D4 flush in a line, the chute over four intact hull walls. Keep those walls: they are the pressure seal.
[*]Load parts through the grabber's Inventory, then select crew beside the D4, press F9 and choose Start / resume pipeline. Right-click a machine for Inventory, Control Panel and Load feed by crew.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosshipbreaker status reports what loaded.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5, Phobos Framework 0.48.0 or newer and Phobos Auto Nav 0.19.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional: Phobos Agriculture, Phobos Manufacturing, Valtora's Ship's Water 0.16.1, Crafting Framework and Salvage Workshop.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Shipbreaker and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those local copies first so only one copy loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
Ordinary saves are supported. Keep required mods installed while a save uses their content. Updating does not refill existing shops or old loot containers.
Processing needs power, output space and cooling; vacuum is not free cooling. Furnace heating and exterior work pause on interruption and wait for Resume. Repeat runs and storage unloading pause on reload; crew loading orders carry on. Capture alone does not permit cutting. Older unclassified residue has no R4 recipe. Since 0.41.0 furnace records settle every two real seconds and before every save, and coolant conduit changes are noticed within two seconds. Automated checks pass; in-game evaluation of recent features is ongoing.

[h2]Credits and sources[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited in the guides. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
NASA Goddard's Raven and ESA's LIRIS experiment (Airbus, Jena Optronik and Sodern) inform the capture sensing research; NIST water data informs the ice thaw energy. The linked guides cite each source beside its claim.
Optional integrations remain their authors' work: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora's Ship's Water[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3789049955]LOGUSS's Common Sense modules[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3788237703]jossla's Study at Terminals[/url].
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production, including PixelLab; the completion cue is original audio. Provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

